; S1a.3.1 — an activator that cannot bind the rule's parameters.
;
; `(pairwise r)` has one argument; `pairwise` declares two parameters. A rule
; name and a property relation may coincide, and a fact that cannot bind the
; parameters does not authorise anything — so `activators_for` filters
; this activator out by ARITY and the rule simply never runs. The
; `CompileError` below is what a caller that builds the pair anyway is told;
; reaching it needs the unfiltered walk (`plan_shape_with(…, false)`).
;
; Until S1.22.0 neither guard existed: the mismatch left every
; parameter-headed premise with an unbound head var, the relation compiler
; dropped them all, and the rule fired unconditionally off an empty plan.
(relation r A B)

(rule pairwise (?R ?T)
  :match  (?R ?a ?b)
  :assert (?T ?b ?a))

(pairwise r)
